<card id="c" title="Gusinje Bus Stop: Where the Bus to Podgorica and Plav Actually Stops">
<do type="prev" label="Back"><prev/></do>
<p>Because the bus does not go that way. There is no bus route straight over the mountains to Podgorica. It loops north through Plav, Berane, Mojkovac and Kolasin, about 195 km of road. Driving the direct way takes under two hours.</p>
<p><b>Tickets</b></p>
<p>Two options. Buy online at <a href="https://busticket4.me/">busticket4.me</a>, which cost me 15.80 euros, and print the ticket before you travel. Or pay the driver in cash when you board. Luggage is 2 euros extra, also to the driver.</p>
<p><b>Worth saying out loud at the stop</b></p>
<p><b>Da li cekate autobus za Podgoricu?</b> — Are you waiting for the bus to Podgorica?</p>
<p><b>Odakle polazi autobus za Podgoricu?</b> — Where does the bus to Podgorica leave from?</p>
<p><b>Quick answers</b></p>
